1787666753196350	seal-dev	itc:v3:AWKZ8kmeSSZmc0AAAAAAQbfVb1VtuwAAAAEwCg		item.create	bn-3rp0	{"description":"Source: #seal thread 01M0GFZFD25HQR58ZBJKEN04MY. Filing failed in message 01M0GG30WP81W282Q9PGWB11RH because the title exceeded 200 characters.\n\nProblem:\nA Git-backed review persists a literal commit SHA in scm_anchor. If an author adds descendant commits, `seal reviews request` only appends a reviewer request. A repeat vote still covers the original SHA. `seal diff` can then report approval_stale=false and uncovered_commits=0 because the review target never moved. Sigil reproduced this with workspace bn-1159, review cr-218gkk, original anchor dfb6aa0, and fixed HEAD 128ce0e. The safe current workaround is a duplicate review.\n\nImplement an audit-logged retarget path for an existing review. Add a ReviewRetargeted event and a `seal reviews retarget` command. Only the review author can retarget an eligible open or approved review. Resolve and persist the new backend-neutral SCM anchor and target commit. Retargeting must invalidate prior approval and require fresh reviewer votes. Do not rewrite events or permit stale approval. Preserve jj behavior and event-source rebuild semantics.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- The command appends ReviewRetargeted with the old and new review targets needed for audit history.\n- Projection rebuilds apply retarget events deterministically.\n- Prior votes or approval do not cover the new target.\n- A fresh vote records and approves the retargeted commit.\n- `seal diff` reports target, stale approval, and uncovered commits correctly before and after retargeting.\n- Invalid states, unauthorized authors, identical targets, and unresolved SCM targets fail with actionable errors and no partial append.\n- Unit and integration tests cover the Git descendant-commit reproduction and projection rebuild.","kind":"task","labels":["feature"],"title":"Add audit-logged review retargeting for Git"}	blake3:2VMJhGwIvwPXnxZbgz0_c-e9akBxvGGrXeaR6XcVU8Q
